<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Werner Munzinger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1832–1875</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Werner Munzinger was a Swiss explorer, linguist and administrator who served the Egyptian government in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. After years in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a> and as governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massawa">Massawa</a>, he was made a pasha. In 1875, leading an Egyptian expedition from Tadjoura towards Shewa, he was killed when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afar">Afar</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aussa">Aussa</a> attacked his column.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/werner-munzinger.jpg" alt="Werner Munzinger" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vollenweider · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WernerMunzinger.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
